<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Frŭsĭno</span></b> ,
			ōnis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of the Hernici</i>, <i>in Latium</i>, <i>situated on the Via
				Latina</i>, now <i>Frosinone</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
			37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 224</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Frŭsĭnas</span></b> ,
				ātis, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Frusino</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				<i>in the neighborhood of Frusino</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 11, 4, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 13, 4</span></i>.—In <i>plur.
				subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Frŭsĭnātes</span></b> ,
			um, m., <i>the inhabitants of
				Frusino</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 10, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 64</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
